   "For years, farmers in the region puzzled over why the same variety of rice grew well in some fields and poorly in others nearby. (1) They tried different seeds, planting dates and amounts of fertiliser, with little effect. (2) Tests eventually showed that the poorer fields lacked a trace element, zinc, that the rice needed in tiny amounts. (3) Adding a small quantity of zinc to those fields raised yields dramatically. (4) The episode showed how a problem can resist solution when people look for it in the wrong place.",
